-- 0031: backfill `inventory.size_std`, and lift misfiled measurements out of
-- `size`. Active rows only (Bhoumik decision, 2026-08-13) — retired history
-- rows keep `size_std` NULL.
--
-- HOW THIS WAS BUILT. 12 subagents classified all 2,783 active
-- (supplier_id, size) pairs against a single shared ruleset
-- (the ingestion SOP's *Size standard*, which was written from it). The grain
-- is the PAIR, not the string: `2.5"` is a caliper at supplier 100 (Quercus,
-- Magnolia — the caliper column already held 2.5) and a pot at supplier 73
-- (Begonia, Narcissus). Each agent saw the pair's row count, sample plant
-- names, and how often height/width/caliper were already populated.
--
-- Three consistency overrides were applied over the agents' output:
--   * supplier 86 (Bold Spring) prints sheared FORM codes — MST, FTG, SST,
--     COL, BOX. `N' BOX` there is not a box; all 6 pairs -> `other`.
--   * a low-confidence DIM reading does NOT move data (47 pairs). It keeps its
--     `size` text and takes `other`, so a human can revisit it.
--   * `0 G` is not a container -> `other`.
--
-- MEASUREMENT MOVES ARE CONSERVATIVE. A value moves only into an EMPTY
-- dimension column, or one already holding the same number (a duplicated
-- caliper). A column holding something DIFFERENT is a conflict: the row is
-- left completely untouched and only gets `size_std = 'other'`. Nothing is
-- overwritten, so no evidence is lost.
--
-- Generated from the agent mapping — see generate.py. Active rows only.

-- height: 356 supplier/size pairs. The value moves only into an EMPTY
-- column, or one already holding the same number (a duplicate); a column
-- holding something different is a conflict and the row is left untouched.
